    "dcf": {
      "holdPeriodMonths": 118,
      "discountRatePercent": 7.75,
      "discountTiming": "monthly",
      "periodConvention": "end",
      "terminalValue": {
        "method": "fixed_value",
        "fixedValue": 147081000,
        "sellingCostsPercent": 0.75,
        "notes": "Residual land-value exit, not capitalized income. Derivation: 27.4 acres = 1,193,544 land SF; 45% FAR = 537,095 buildable SF; land value of $185 per buildable SF today, grown at 4%/yr over the hold = $273.85 per buildable SF at exit; 537,095 x $273.85 = ~$147.08M. The land basis exceeds the capitalized-income alternative (~$138M at a 5.75% cap on marked-to-market NOI), so the land approach is adopted. ORE v0.1 has no structured land-residual terminal method; fixed_value carries the conclusion and this note carries the math so any reader can reproduce it."
      },
      "notes": "Hold period is 118 months so the exit lands exactly at the 2036-04-30 lease expiration — contract rent for the full hold, land value at the end, no rollover modeled. Going-in yield ~6.2% on year-1 NOI. IRR convention note: the underwriting source computed IRR on annual end-of-year cash flows; the ORE engine's monthly-compounded IRR reads roughly 25-30 bps higher on identical cash flows."
    },
